{"seq":20,"trial_id":"matrix-mu-2026-11/hermes-opus-none-mu-v03-dev/sy-03-marrow-fieldworks-ticket-numbers/r1","wall_ts":"2026-11-05T08:22:30.263Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-16T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"dfc56b04164dd8db793e46341b7ec9a4f1bd66b586155e436614867ce4222b46","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DMATRIX0001","text":"Hi Pree, here's what I found on Marrow Fieldworks. I checked Moss's public notes, #central-random, #central-team, and the other channels you're in for this week.\n\nTickets on Marrow Fieldworks:\n1. PD-5302: a follow-up from this week. Hollis posted it in #central-random on Wed 14 Oct and named Marrow Fieldworks directly.\n2. #4409: recurring timeout on the Gatehouse Check-In report at the Salina North yard (Bay 4 and the west grain-bin apron, during the 06:00 flatbed intake). From Moss's note \"Central handoffs next week\" (2 Jan 2026).\n3. #4412: driver SMS prompt glitch when staging combine trailers on unpaved overflow lots. Same Moss note.\n\nOne caveat on #4409 and #4412: Moss lists them under the Marrow Fieldworks handoff as tickets on \"Pree's dealer account.\" The note never puts the name and the ticket numbers in the same sentence, so I'm reading that as Marrow Fieldworks.\n\nPossibly related:\n- #8841: in #central-random on 13 Oct, Tobias said he'd flagged West yard Door 2 double-booking on this ticket. Hollis called that \"Tobias's dealer account.\" Since Marrow Fieldworks changed hands in January, this could be the same account, but nothing says so, so I've left it off the main list.\n\nNot Marrow Fieldworks (these are Marrow Agrisupply, so don't mix them up): FR-882 from Moss's note and PD-4821 from #central-team in June.\n\nThis week's chat in #central-team, #general, #help-it-ops and #inc-tansley-carrier-api had no other Marrow Fieldworks tickets. I couldn't find any account ticket files in the share to check against."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DMATRIX0001","ts":"1792159200.000127"}}
{"seq":21,"trial_id":"matrix-mu-2026-11/hermes-opus-none-mu-v03-dev/sy-03-marrow-fieldworks-ticket-numbers/r1","wall_ts":"2026-11-05T08:22:38.775Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-16T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"b278f196303248dd277af6519203298876792464b9e1b701f5cb4d0993536cc5","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DMATRIX0001","text":"I sent Pree her list in our DM. I found three Marrow Fieldworks ticket numbers, and only one of them is named as Marrow Fieldworks outright.\n\n1. PD-5302 comes from #central-random. On 14 Oct Hollis posted it as a Marrow Fieldworks follow-up from this week.\n2. #4409 comes from Moss's note \"Central handoffs next week\" (2 Jan 2026). It's a recurring timeout on the gatehouse check-in report at the Salina North yard.\n3. #4412 comes from the same note. It's a glitch in the text prompts drivers get when staging combine trailers on unpaved overflow lots.\n\nThe note doesn't actually name Marrow Fieldworks next to #4409 and #4412. It lists them under the Marrow Fieldworks handoff as tickets on \"Pree's dealer account\", so I told her I'm treating them as Marrow Fieldworks.\n\nI gave her two more things to watch:\n- #8841 might belong to the same account, but I left it off the list. Tobias flagged it in #central-random on 13 Oct, and Hollis called it \"Tobias's dealer account\". Marrow Fieldworks changed hands in January, so it could be the same account, but nothing says so.\n- FR-882 and PD-4821 belong to Marrow Agrisupply, a different account, so she shouldn't mix them up.\n\nI only read channels she's a member of and public files, and I didn't use the company-wide message search. This week's messages in #central-team, #general, #help-it-ops and #inc-tansley-carrier-api had no other Marrow Fieldworks tickets. There are no ticket files in the shared files she can see, so I couldn't check any of these against the account's own records."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DMATRIX0001","ts":"1792